From: nuubOS Project <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw88: leave LPS on light traffic, re-enter after quiet periods

rtw88 keeps the radio out of LPS only while a 2 s watchdog period sees
more than 50 unicast frames in one direction. In LPS the AP holds
downlink frames until the next beacon, so a transfer that starts while
the radio is in LPS slows down to a few frames per period and never
crosses the threshold again: on the RTL8821CS (SDIO) an scp upload ran
at ~6 KB/s with round trips up to 380 ms, and at full speed at once with
power save off.

Count both directions together, leave LPS from 8 frames per period
(about 4 per second) and enter it again only after 3 quiet periods in a
row (6 s), so a transfer does not flap in and out of LPS. An idle link
carries almost no unicast data and still enters LPS.

Signed-off-by: nuubOS Project <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/ps.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/ps.h
@@ -5,7 +5,14 @@
 #ifndef __RTW_PS_H_
 #define __RTW_PS_H_
 
-#define RTW_LPS_THRESHOLD	50
+/* Unicast data frames (tx + rx) per watchdog period (2 s) that keep the
+ * radio out of LPS, and the quiet periods needed before entering it again.
+ * In LPS the AP holds downlink frames until the next beacon: a transfer
+ * slows down to a few frames per period, so a high threshold never lets
+ * it leave LPS again.
+ */
+#define RTW_LPS_TRAFFIC_MIN	8
+#define RTW_LPS_IDLE_PERIODS	3
 
 #define POWER_MODE_ACK		BIT(6)
 #define POWER_MODE_PG		BIT(4)
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/main.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/main.h
@@ -2083,6 +2083,7 @@
 	/* watch dog every 2 sec */
 	struct delayed_work watch_dog_work;
 	u32 watch_dog_cnt;
+	u8 lps_idle_periods;
 
 	struct list_head rsvd_page_list;
 
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/main.c
@@ -248,11 +248,11 @@
 	if (busy_traffic != test_bit(RTW_FLAG_BUSY_TRAFFIC, rtwdev->flags))
 		rtw_coex_wl_status_change_notify(rtwdev, 0);
 
-	if (stats->tx_cnt > RTW_LPS_THRESHOLD ||
-	    stats->rx_cnt > RTW_LPS_THRESHOLD)
-		ps_active = true;
-	else
-		ps_active = false;
+	if (stats->tx_cnt + stats->rx_cnt >= RTW_LPS_TRAFFIC_MIN)
+		rtwdev->lps_idle_periods = 0;
+	else if (rtwdev->lps_idle_periods < RTW_LPS_IDLE_PERIODS)
+		rtwdev->lps_idle_periods++;
+	ps_active = rtwdev->lps_idle_periods < RTW_LPS_IDLE_PERIODS;
 
 	tx_unicast_mbps = stats->tx_unicast >> RTW_TP_SHIFT;
 	rx_unicast_mbps = stats->rx_unicast >> RTW_TP_SHIFT;
